IMPORT prelude

-- Presidential Elections Act 1991 (Singapore) -- what happens when a reserved election fails (s 5B), who gets a certificate of
-- eligibility (ss 8(3), 8A, 8B), notice of nomination (s 7), the candidate's deposit (s 10), compulsory voting and the $50 to get back
-- on the register (s 26), the election expenses cap (ss 50, 61), the employer's duty on polling day (s 58), and the polling-day and
-- campaign-period publication offences (ss 42C, 59, 60B, 60C, 60D, 62).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021), informal consolidation, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/PrEA1991.txt ("Current version as at 01 Oct 2026" per the deposit's metadata), with amendments to
-- Act 34 of 2024 (in force 22 January 2025) and S 612/2023 shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a candidate, a voter, an
-- employer or a publisher meets. Not encoded: the community requirement and service requirements themselves (they are in Articles
-- 19 and 19B of the Constitution, which is not deposited here and is not read), the Community Committee's procedure, nomination and
-- polling procedure, DRE voting, overseas and postal voting, the corrupt practices (ss 38 to 42), the election advertising regime
-- beyond the cooling-off ban (ss 42B, 42E to 42R), election agents and returns (ss 43 to 57), and election petitions (Parts 4, 5).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Presidential Elections Act 1991 -- elections`

§§ `5B and 7A(4) -- when an election wholly fails, and what the next writ is`

-- s 5B(1): if an election reserved for ONE community "wholly fails, elections under all subsequent writs are to be open elections
-- until a person is elected as President".
-- s 5B(2): reserved for 2 communities -- Article 19B(2)(b)(i) applies; if that fails, (b)(ii) applies under the next writ; if that
-- fails too, all subsequent writs are open.
-- s 5B(3): reserved for 3 communities -- (c)(i), then (c)(ii), then (c)(iii) under the third writ, then open.
-- s 5B(4): "a person does not need to belong to any community to be elected as President in an open election" under s 5B.
-- s 5B(5): "an election under a writ is deemed to have wholly failed ONLY if no person stands or will stand nominated as a candidate
-- on nomination day."
-- s 7A(4), by contrast: "an election shall have wholly failed if no candidate is nominated OR RETURNED AS ELECTED".
-- (What each limb of Article 19B(2) requires is in the Constitution and is not encoded; the stages are named by their order.)
DECLARE `Next writ` IS ONE OF
    `the first rule for the reserved election`
    `the second rule for the reserved election`
    `the third rule for the reserved election`
    `an open election`

GIVEN `communities reserved for` IS A NUMBER, `writs wholly failed so far` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Next writ`
`the rule under the next writ` MEANS
    IF `writs wholly failed so far` AT LEAST `communities reserved for`
        THEN `an open election`
        ELSE IF `writs wholly failed so far` EQUALS 0
                THEN `the first rule for the reserved election`
                ELSE IF `writs wholly failed so far` EQUALS 1
                        THEN `the second rule for the reserved election`
                        ELSE `the third rule for the reserved election`

GIVEN `communities reserved for` IS A NUMBER, `writs wholly failed so far` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the winner need not belong to any community` IF
    `the rule under the next writ` `communities reserved for` `writs wholly failed so far` EQUALS `an open election`

GIVEN `persons nominated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the election wholly failed for section 5B` IF
    `persons nominated` EQUALS 0

GIVEN `persons nominated` IS A NUMBER, `someone returned as elected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the election wholly failed for section 7A` IF
    `persons nominated` EQUALS 0 OR (NOT `someone returned as elected`)

§§ `7 -- notice of nomination`

-- s 7: the Returning Officer must publish notice of the writ and of nomination in the Gazette "at least 4 clear days before
-- nomination day". (Reading "clear days" as excluding both the day of publication and nomination day is an INFERENCE; the Act does
-- not define it.) Days are counted as day numbers.
GIVEN `day of Gazette notice` IS A NUMBER, `nomination day number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice was given in time` IF
    `nomination day number` MINUS `day of Gazette notice` MINUS 1 AT LEAST 4

§§ `8(3), 8A, 8B -- certificate of eligibility`

-- s 8(3): an applicant "below 45 years of age as at nomination day or, if there is more than one nomination day, the latest of those
-- days" -- the Committee need not consider the application and it "is deemed to be withdrawn" (Act 9 of 2023).
-- s 8A(1): the Committee MUST issue a certificate if satisfied (a) of "integrity, good character and reputation" and (b) the service
-- requirements in Article 19(2)(g) are met; (2)(a) it MAY reject an application not made according to the Act; (b) it MUST reject
-- if no community declaration was submitted; (3) including, in a reserved election, where the declaration does not state that the
-- applicant considers himself or herself a member of the reserved community.
-- s 8B: decision "no later than the day before nomination day". s 8C: the certificate is conclusive and "not subject to appeal or
-- review in any court".
GIVEN `age at the latest nomination day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is deemed withdrawn` IF
    `age at the latest nomination day` LESS THAN 45

GIVEN `submitted a community declaration` IS A BOOLEAN, `the election is reserved` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `declared membership of the reserved community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee must reject` IF
        (NOT `submitted a community declaration`)
    OR  (`the election is reserved` AND (NOT `declared membership of the reserved community`))

GIVEN `age at the latest nomination day` IS A NUMBER, `satisfied of integrity, character and reputation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `satisfied of the service requirements` IS A BOOLEAN, `submitted a community declaration` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the election is reserved` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared membership of the reserved community` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made according to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee must issue a certificate of eligibility` IF
        (NOT `the application is deemed withdrawn` `age at the latest nomination day`)
    AND (NOT `the Committee must reject` `submitted a community declaration` `the election is reserved` `declared membership of the reserved community`)
    AND `made according to the Act`
    AND `satisfied of integrity, character and reputation`
    AND `satisfied of the service requirements`

GIVEN `decision day` IS A NUMBER, `nomination day number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee decided in time` IF
    `decision day` AT MOST `nomination day number` MINUS 1

§§ `10 -- the candidate's deposit`

-- s 10(1): "a sum equal to 3 times the amount of deposit referred to in section 28(1) of the Parliamentary Elections Act 1954",
-- between the writ and 12 noon of nomination day; (1A) in default the candidate "is deemed to have withdrawn".
-- (4) returned if not nominated, the election wholly failed, or the candidate withdraws; (4A) returned if the candidate dies before
-- the poll; (5) "If a candidate who has made the required deposit is not elected and the number of votes polled by the candidate does
-- NOT EXCEED ONE-EIGHTH of the total number of votes polled, the amount deposited is forfeited"; (5A) otherwise returned;
-- (6)(a) votes polled means votes counted other than rejected votes.
-- (The Parliamentary Elections Act figure is not read here; it is a parameter.)
GIVEN `the Parliamentary Elections Act deposit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the presidential deposit` MEANS
    3 TIMES `the Parliamentary Elections Act deposit`

GIVEN `paid by noon on nomination day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is deemed to have withdrawn` IF
    NOT `paid by noon on nomination day`

GIVEN `the candidate was elected` IS A BOOLEAN, `the candidate's valid votes` IS A NUMBER, `total valid votes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposit is forfeited` IF
    (NOT `the candidate was elected`) AND `the candidate's valid votes` TIMES 8 AT MOST `total valid votes`

§§ `26 -- compulsory voting`

-- s 26(1): "Every elector must record his or her vote". (2) the Returning Officer lists those who failed to vote; (5) their names are
-- "expunged from the register of electors"; (7) they may apply for restoration; (8) with "a good and sufficient reason" the name is
-- restored "without penalty", otherwise "on payment to the Registration Officer of a sum of $50"; (11) after a writ is issued no name
-- may be restored "until after nomination day or, if a poll is to be taken, until after polling day".
GIVEN `had a good and sufficient reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum to be restored to the register` MEANS
    IF `had a good and sufficient reason` THEN 0 ELSE 50

GIVEN `a writ has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN, `a poll is to be taken` IS A BOOLEAN, `nomination day has passed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `polling day has passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a name may be restored now` IF
    IF NOT `a writ has been issued`
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE IF `a poll is to be taken`
                THEN `polling day has passed`
                ELSE `nomination day has passed`

§§ `50 and 61 -- election expenses`

-- s 50(1): no candidate or election agent may spend "in excess of $600,000 or an amount equal to 30 cents for each elector on the
-- registers, whichever is the greater". (1A) the amount does not include "personal expenses, or any fee paid to any election agent not
-- exceeding $500". (Read literally: an agent's fee of $500 or less is left out; a larger fee is counted in full. That reading is a
-- choice -- the text could also mean the first $500 of any fee is left out.) (2) knowingly exceeding it is an illegal practice.
-- s 61(1): illegal practice -- fine up to $2,000 and incapable for 3 years of being registered, voting, or being elected President or
-- an MP; (2) prosecution needs the Public Prosecutor's consent.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `electors on the registers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the expenses cap` MEANS
    `the greater of` 600000 (`electors on the registers` TIMES 30 DIVIDED BY 100)

GIVEN `total spent` IS A NUMBER, `personal expenses` IS A NUMBER, `agent's fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the counted expenses` MEANS
    IF `agent's fee` AT MOST 500
    THEN `total spent` MINUS `personal expenses` MINUS `agent's fee`
    ELSE `total spent` MINUS `personal expenses`

GIVEN `electors on the registers` IS A NUMBER, `total spent` IS A NUMBER, `personal expenses` IS A NUMBER,
      `agent's fee` IS A NUMBER, `acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `overspending is an illegal practice` IF
        `acted knowingly`
    AND `the counted expenses` `total spent` `personal expenses` `agent's fee` GREATER THAN `the expenses cap` `electors on the registers`

GIVEN `years since conviction for an illegal practice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `still barred from voting or standing` IF
    `years since conviction for an illegal practice` LESS THAN 3

§§ `58 -- the employer on polling day`

-- s 58(1): every employer must allow every elector employed "a reasonable period for voting"; (1A) no deduction from pay and no
-- penalty for that absence; (2) refusing or interfering -- fine up to $1,000 or 6 months or both.
GIVEN `allowed a reasonable period to vote` IS A BOOLEAN, `deducted pay for the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is in breach` IF
    (NOT `allowed a reasonable period to vote`) OR `deducted pay for the absence`

§§ `42C, 59, 60B, 60C, 60D, 62 -- the calendar of publication offences`

-- s 60B(1): no publishing of election survey results "during the period beginning with the day the writ of election is issued ... and
-- ending with the close of all polling stations on polling day".
-- s 60C(1): no exit-poll statements or forecasts "on polling day ... before the close of all polling stations".
-- s 42C(4): the "cooling-off period" runs from "the eve of polling day" to "the close of polling on polling day"; election advertising
-- is banned in it ($1,000 or 12 months).
-- s 62(1): no canvassing, and no visiting an elector at home or work, "on polling day and the eve of polling day" ($1,500 or 12
-- months). s 59(1): no badges, flags, posters etc. as political propaganda "on polling day or on the eve of polling day" ($1,000 or 12
-- months), (4) except a candidate wearing a replica of his or her own symbol.
-- s 60D(1): defence to 60B / 60C if the person proves BOTH (a) circumstances beyond his or her control and (b) all reasonable steps and
-- due diligence.
-- (s 62 and s 59 are not limited to before the close of polls; read literally they cover the whole of polling day.)
DECLARE Moment IS ONE OF
    `before the writ`
    `after the writ, before the eve of polling day`
    `the eve of polling day`
    `polling day before the polls close`
    `polling day after the polls close`

GIVEN `the moment` IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `survey results may not be published` IF
    CONSIDER `the moment`
    WHEN `after the writ, before the eve of polling day` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the eve of polling day` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `polling day before the polls close` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the moment` IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exit polls may not be published` IF
    `the moment` EQUALS `polling day before the polls close`

GIVEN `the moment` IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is the cooling-off period` IF
    `the moment` EQUALS `the eve of polling day` OR `the moment` EQUALS `polling day before the polls close`

GIVEN `the moment` IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `canvassing is banned` IF
    CONSIDER `the moment`
    WHEN `the eve of polling day` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `polling day before the polls close` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `polling day after the polls close` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the moment` IS A Moment, `a candidate wearing a replica of own symbol` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `displaying a party badge is an offence` IF
    `canvassing is banned` `the moment` AND (NOT `a candidate wearing a replica of own symbol`)

GIVEN `beyond the person's control` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable steps and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 60D defence succeeds` IF
    `beyond the person's control` AND `took all reasonable steps and due diligence`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `employer refusing time to vote`
    `party badge on polling day or eve`
    `publishing survey results in the blackout`
    `publishing an exit poll`
    `canvassing on polling day or eve`
    `election advertising in the cooling-off period`
    `an illegal practice`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `employer refusing time to vote` THEN 1000
    WHEN `party badge on polling day or eve` THEN 1000
    WHEN `publishing survey results in the blackout` THEN 1500
    WHEN `publishing an exit poll` THEN 1500
    WHEN `canvassing on polling day or eve` THEN 1500
    WHEN `election advertising in the cooling-off period` THEN 1000
    WHEN `an illegal practice` THEN 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `employer refusing time to vote` THEN 6
    WHEN `an illegal practice` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 12
